// while_loop.gopi
// Expected: 1 diagnostic (SEMANTIC) — "variable 'x' might not have been
// assigned a value", on the final show(x). A loop's body might execute zero
// times (conservatively, even here, where the condition happens to be a
// literal `yes`), so an assignment made only inside it is never considered
// definite afterward. The read/write of x INSIDE the loop body itself is
// fine — sequential assignment within the same block.

none main() {
    num x;
    loop (yes) {
        x = 5;
        show(x);
    }
    show(x);
}
